# happy-birthday-esp32 Project Context

ESP32 Arduino-framework birthday gift device: animated TFT display + passive buzzer melody + button trigger.

## Stack
- **Framework**: Arduino on ESP32 (PlatformIO, not ESP-IDF)
- **Display**: ST7735 1.8" SPI TFT 128x160 via `TFT_eSPI` library
- **Buzzer**: passive piezo on GPIO25, driven with `tone()`
- **Build tool**: PlatformIO (`pio run`, `pio run -t upload`)
- **Config**: display pins and driver set via `build_flags` in `platformio.ini` — no `User_Setup.h`

## Pin mapping
| Signal | GPIO |
|---|---|
| TFT CS | 5 |
| TFT DC | 16 |
| TFT RST | 17 |
| TFT SCK | 18 |
| TFT MOSI | 23 |
| Buzzer | 25 |
| Button | 14 |
| Boot btn | 0 |

## Asset pipeline
- PNGs must be exactly **128x160**
- Convert: `python3 scripts/png_to_rgb565.py <in.png> <out.h> <array_name>`
- Font: `python3 scripts/ttf_to_gfx.py <in.ttf> <out.h> <size_px>`
- Frame registry: `include/cake_frames.h` — update when adding/removing frames
- Always keep `tft.setSwapBytes(true)` — generated arrays are big-endian RGB565

## Melody format
```cpp
struct Note { uint16_t freq; uint16_t ms; };
const Note melody[] = { {freq_hz, duration_ms}, ... };
// Use {0, ms} for rests
```

## Flash upload quirk
This board needs manual download mode if auto-reset fails:
hold BOOT → run upload → release BOOT when "Writing at 0x..." appears.

## Power
- DevKit VIN pin accepts 4.5–12V (onboard AMS1117 regulator → 3.3V)
- Single 3.7V LiPo works on VIN (3.7–4.2V gives enough regulator headroom)
- Use physical power switch on VIN/battery+ line for battery builds
